==History==
2024
*The Battle Ram's Evolution card was added to the game on 1/4/2024, in the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (1/4/2024)|April 2024 Update]].
*On 14/5/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (14/5/2024)|Balance Update]], increased the [[Barbarians/Evolution|Evolved Barbarians]]' attack speed boost to 3 seconds (from 2 seconds), decreased the Evolved Barbarians' hitpoints to 110% of the originals' (from 125%), and removed the Evolved Battle Ram's ability to push back large [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]].
*On 2/10/2024, the [[Version History#Lucky Drops 2.0 Update (2/10/2024)|Lucky Drops 2.0 Update]], fixed a bug where the Evolved Battle Ram would deal no damage to large troops.
*On 16/12/2024, the [[Version History#2024 Quarter 4 Update (16/12/2024)|2024 Quarter 4 Update]], added a sound effect to the Evolved Barbarians after death.
2025
*On 31/3/2024, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Evolved Battle Ram's hitpoints by 0.1% and its charge damage by 0.17%. It also fixed a bug where Evolved Barbarians would not spawn after being buffed by [[Royal Chef]].
*On 6/10/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2025)=|Balance Update]] decreased the Rage's speed boost to 30% (from 35%).

==Trivia==
*A [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battering_ram battering ram] is a siege engine that originated in ancient times and was designed to break open the masonry walls of fortifications or splinter their wooden gates. In its simplest form, a battering ram is just a large, heavy log carried by several people and propelled with force against an obstacle; the ram would be sufficient to damage the target if the log were massive enough and/or it were moved quickly enough. The earliest depiction of a possible battering ram is from the tomb of the 11th Dynasty noble Khety, where a pair of soldiers advance towards a fortress under the protection of a mobile roofed structure, carrying a long pole that may represent a simple battering ram.
**In the German, Norwegian, Turkish, Indonesian and Finnish language settings of the game, the Battle Ram's name translates to "Battering Ram". In the Japanese, Chinese, Persian, Malaysian, Thai, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Battle Ram's name translates to "Siege Barbarian", "Barbarian Battering Ram", "Battle Tower", "Crasher", "Fight Bumper", and "Castle Breaking Weapon" respectively.
**The head of the Evolved Battle Ram resembles that of the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Wall_Wrecker Level 3 Wall Wrecker] from Clash of Clans.
*The Battle Ram’s Evolution is 1 of 2 evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] with a charge, the other being [[Royal Recruits/Evolution|Royal Recruits]].
*The Battle Ram's Evolution is the only evolved [[Cards|card]] that can spawn another evolved card, that being [[Barbarians/Evolution|Evolved Barbarians]].
*The Battle Ram's Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
**It is also 1 of 4 evolved card whose regular card is not the subject of any Emote, the others being Royal Recruits, [[Zap/Evolution|Zap]], and [[Giant Snowball/Evolution|Giant Snowball]].

